IMPORT prelude

-- National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009 (Commonwealth of Australia), with the National Credit Code (Schedule 1) --
-- what a lender must do before lending to me, what a small amount loan may cost me, what happens when I cannot pay, and
-- whether an unlicensed lender can hold me to the loan.
--
-- SEAT: the borrower (the consumer, the debtor, the mortgagor) -- "Must the lender check I can afford this? Is this loan
-- unsuitable for me? What may I be charged on a payday loan, and what do I not owe? If I cannot pay, what must the lender
-- do before it comes after me? Can an unlicensed lender enforce the loan?". Every exported question is that person's.
-- Where the Act hands a judgment to someone else (the licensee's reasonable inquiries, what is "likely", the credit
-- provider reasonably believing something, the court considering an order appropriate), it is asked as a fact, and the
-- answer is conditional on it.
--
-- Provisions covered. The Act: s 5(1) "small amount credit contract", "short-term credit contract"; s 6(1) item 1 (credit
-- activity: the credit provider limbs); s 29(1), (3), (4) (no credit activity without a licence); s 32(1) (no fee for
-- unlicensed activity); s 128 (assess within 90 days, or the prescribed period); s 129; s 130(1), (1A) (inquiries and
-- verification); s 131(2), (3), (3AA); s 132(2), (4) (my copy of the assessment, free); s 133(1), (2), (3), (3AA), (5)
-- (unsuitable contracts forbidden); s 133BA(1); s 133BE(1), (5) (no credit limit increase invitations); s 133CA(1) (no
-- short-term credit contracts); s 133CC(1), (3) (small amount repayments within the prescribed income limit); s 180(1)-(4)
-- (court orders for unlicensed lending). The National Credit Code: ss 5(1), (3), (4) (when the Code applies); s 7(1);
-- s 23A (no interest on a small amount credit contract); s 31A (the 20% and 4% caps); s 31B(1)-(3); s 31C (unexpired
-- monthly fees); s 39B (twice the adjusted credit amount after default); ss 42, 43 (the mortgage document); s 72(1)-(5)
-- (hardship notice, and the table of periods for the lender's answer); s 73(1), (1A) (written notice of the change);
-- s 88(1), (3), (5), (6) (the default notice and its 30 days); s 89 (remedying the default); s 89A (hardship notice holds
-- off enforcement).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 52, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 57, 2026 (register id
-- C2026C00340), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2009A00134.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026).
-- Regulations used: National Consumer Credit Protection Regulations 2010, Compilation No. 57, compilation date 5 September
-- 2026, includes amendments F2026L01157 (register id F2026C00861), as deposited at
-- ../../../national-consumer-credit-protection-regulations-2010/registers/source-bundle/F2010L00631.txt (retrieved 19
-- October 2026): reg 4D (the $2,000 small amount ceiling raised by fees included in the credit), reg 28HB (social security
-- recipients: Services Australia statements), reg 28J (120 days for a home purchase secured by a mortgage), reg 28JA (the
-- maximum credit limit I require), reg 28LCA (small amount repayments at most 10% of available income), reg 28LCF (split
-- small and medium contracts are unsuitable).
-- NOT DEPOSITED: the ASIC legislative instrument under s 160F (the period in which a card's limit must be repayable). What I
-- could repay within it is an INPUT. The maximum chargeable under a single contract under Code s 32A (reg 28LCF(2)(c)) is
-- an INPUT; s 32A is not encoded.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the licensing regime (Part 2-2) and credit representatives; credit assistance (Part 3-1, including s 124A
-- except as a ground in s 180); standard home loans (Part 3-2A); Key Facts Sheets (ss 133BB-133BD); reverse mortgages; the
-- rest of Part 3-2C (ss 133CB, 133CD); comprehensive credit reporting; consumer leases; the Code's disclosure, interest,
-- comparison rate and unjust transactions provisions; Code s 6 exclusions (short term credit of 62 days or less and the
-- rest); medium amount credit contracts and the s 32A cap; default fees and government charges under s 31A(1)(c), (d);
-- postponement requests (s 94), court changes (s 74), acceleration clauses (s 93), repossession of goods (s 91);
-- penalties and the dollar value of a penalty unit; ASIC and AFCA. Whether a contract is a continuing or low cost credit
-- contract (Code s 204, Act s 5) is an INPUT. A credit report (c043) is the Privacy Act 1988, Part IIIA; registration of
-- the mortgage (c052) is the Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA); the paint and the glue (k063) are the WA Criminal Code and the
-- Restraining Orders Act 1997 (WA).
--
-- DATES are numbers YYYYMMDD (1 March 2037 is 20370301). The N-th anniversary of day D is D + N x 10000. "Within 2 years
-- of" a day is read as before its second anniversary; the period that "ends 7 years after" a day as including the seventh
-- anniversary; "within 6 years of the day" as before the sixth anniversary. Periods in days (the default notice, the
-- hardship table) are counted by the caller and given as numbers of days. A year is 365 days for a small amount credit
-- contract's term. These are the encoder's conventions, not the Act's.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009 -- from the seat of the borrower`

§§ `ss 6 item 1, 29, 32 -- is the person lending to me or collecting from me licensed`

-- s 6(1) item 1: a person engages in a credit activity if "(a) the person is a credit provider under a credit contract; or
-- (b) the person carries on a business of providing credit, being credit the provision of which the National Credit Code
-- applies to; or (c) the person performs the obligations, or exercises the rights, of a credit provider in relation to a
-- credit contract or proposed credit contract (whether the person does so as the credit provider or on behalf of the credit
-- provider)". (Items 2-5 -- credit services, consumer leases, mortgages, guarantees -- are not encoded.)
-- s 29(1): "A person must not engage in a credit activity if the person does not hold a licence authorising the person to
-- engage in the credit activity." Civil penalty: 5,000 penalty units. (2): offence, 2 years imprisonment.
-- (3): a defence if the person acts "on behalf of another person (the principal)", is an "employee or director" of the
-- principal (or of a related body corporate) or a "credit representative" of the principal, acts "within the authority of
-- the principal", and "the principal holds a licence". (4): the same for a representative of a principal exempted under
-- s 109 or s 110.
-- s 32(1): a person must not "demand, receive or accept any fee, charge or other amount from a consumer for engaging in a
-- credit activity if, by engaging in that credit activity, the person contravenes, or would contravene, section 29".
DECLARE `Lender or collector` HAS
    `is the credit provider under my credit contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carries on a business of providing credit to which the Code applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exercises a credit provider's rights against me, for itself or on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a licence authorising the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts within authority as employee, director or credit representative of a licensed principal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts within authority as representative of a principal exempted under s 109 or s 110` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A `Lender or collector`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `engages in a credit activity` IF
        `the person`'s `is the credit provider under my credit contract`
    OR  `the person`'s `carries on a business of providing credit to which the Code applies`
    OR  `the person`'s `exercises a credit provider's rights against me, for itself or on its behalf`

@export Is the person lending to me, or collecting the loan from me, doing it without the licence the Act requires (s 29)?
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Lender or collector` @desc The lender, or the person collecting or enforcing the loan for a lender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the person dealing with me without a licence` IF
        `engages in a credit activity` `the person`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `holds a licence authorising the activity`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `acts within authority as employee, director or credit representative of a licensed principal`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `acts within authority as representative of a principal exempted under s 109 or s 110`)

@export May this person demand or take any fee or charge from me for the loan (s 32)?
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Lender or collector` @desc The lender, or the person collecting or enforcing the loan for a lender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the person take a fee from me` IF
    NOT (`Is the person dealing with me without a licence` `the person`)

§§ `s 180 -- can I ask the court not to enforce an unlicensed lender's contract`

-- s 180(1): if "(a) a person (the defendant) engages in a credit activity in relation to another person (the plaintiff); and
-- (b) the engaging in the activity contravenes ... (i) section 29 ...; (ii) section 124A ...; (iii) section 133CA", the
-- court "may make such order as the court considers appropriate". (2) examples: "(a) an order declaring the whole or any
-- part of a contract ... to be void"; "(c) an order refusing to enforce any or all of the terms of such a contract"; "(d)
-- an order directing the defendant to refund money or return property". (3): "only if: (a) the plaintiff or ASIC (on
-- behalf of the plaintiff) applies ...; and (b) the application is made within 6 years of the day the cause of action ...
-- accrued". (4): ASIC only "if the plaintiff has given consent in writing before the application is made".
-- The Act does not make an unlicensed lender's contract void or unenforceable of itself. The court MAY, on an application
-- by the person the credit activity was engaged in relation to, or by ASIC with that person's written consent, in time.
-- Which order it makes is the court's judgment: this answers only whether the court can make one.
DECLARE `My application to the court` HAS
    `the lender engaged in the credit activity in relation to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the activity contravened s 29, s 124A or s 133CA` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made by me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made by ASIC with my prior written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cause of action accrued on` IS A NUMBER
    `made on` IS A NUMBER

@export Can the court make orders on my application against an unlicensed lender, such as refusing to enforce the contract or ordering a refund (s 180)?
GIVEN `the application` IS A `My application to the court` @desc Your (or ASIC's) application to the court, with dates as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court make orders against the lender for me` IF
        `the application`'s `the lender engaged in the credit activity in relation to me`
    AND `the application`'s `the activity contravened s 29, s 124A or s 133CA`
    AND (`the application`'s `made by me` OR `the application`'s `made by ASIC with my prior written consent`)
    AND `the application`'s `made on` LESS THAN `the application`'s `cause of action accrued on` PLUS 60000

§§ `Code ss 5, 7, 42, 43 -- does the Code cover my loan, and is my mortgage enforceable`

-- Code s 5(1): the Code applies if, when the contract is entered into, "(a) the debtor is a natural person or a strata
-- corporation; and (b) the credit is provided or intended to be provided wholly or predominantly: (i) for personal,
-- domestic or household purposes; or (ii) to purchase, renovate or improve residential property for investment purposes;
-- or (iii) to refinance" such investment credit; "(c) a charge is or may be made for providing the credit; and (d) the
-- credit provider provides the credit in the course of a business of providing credit carried on in this jurisdiction or
-- as part of or incidentally to any other business". (3): "investment by the debtor is not a personal, domestic or
-- household purpose". (4): the predominant purpose is "(a) the purpose for which more than half of the credit is intended
-- to be used". Whether a purpose is personal, domestic or household is not defined: it is asked as a fact (the amount).
-- The exclusions in s 6 (short term credit, pawnbrokers, employee loans and so on) are not encoded.
DECLARE `My credit` HAS
    `I am a natural person or strata corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount of credit` IS A NUMBER
    `amount for personal, domestic or household purposes or residential investment property` IS A NUMBER
    `a charge is or may be made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lender provides it in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Does the National Credit Code cover my loan (Code s 5)?
GIVEN `the credit` IS A `My credit` @desc Your loan, with the amounts in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Code cover my loan` IF
        `the credit`'s `I am a natural person or strata corporation`
    AND `the credit`'s `amount for personal, domestic or household purposes or residential investment property` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `the credit`'s `amount of credit`
    AND `the credit`'s `a charge is or may be made`
    AND `the credit`'s `the lender provides it in the course of a business`

-- Code s 7(1): the Code applies to a mortgage if "(a) it secures obligations under a credit contract or a related guarantee;
-- and (b) the mortgagor is a natural person or a strata corporation".
-- s 42(1): "A mortgage must be in the form of a written mortgage document that is signed by the mortgagor." (2): it is
-- enough if "(a) the mortgage is contained in a credit contract signed by the mortgagor" or one of the documents is signed
-- and refers to the others. (4): "A mortgage is not enforceable unless it complies with this section." ((3), goods
-- mortgages, not encoded.)
-- s 43(1): "If a mortgage is in the form of a written mortgage document and is not part of a credit contract, the credit
-- provider must give the mortgagor a copy to keep ... within 14 days after it is made." (2): not if already given.
DECLARE `My mortgage` HAS
    `secures obligations under a credit contract or related guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a natural person or strata corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a written mortgage document I signed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is contained in a credit contract I signed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have already been given a copy to keep` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the mortgage` IS A `My mortgage`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Code applies to the mortgage` IF
        `the mortgage`'s `secures obligations under a credit contract or related guarantee`
    AND `the mortgage`'s `I am a natural person or strata corporation`

@export Is my mortgage enforceable as far as the National Credit Code is concerned (Code s 42)?
GIVEN `the mortgage` IS A `My mortgage` @desc The mortgage over your property
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my mortgage enforceable under the Code` IF
        (NOT `the Code applies to the mortgage` `the mortgage`)
    OR  `the mortgage`'s `is a written mortgage document I signed`
    OR  `the mortgage`'s `is contained in a credit contract I signed`

@export Within how many days after it is made must my lender give me a copy of my mortgage (0 if no copy is owed) (Code s 43)?
GIVEN `the mortgage` IS A `My mortgage` @desc The mortgage over your property
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Days for my lender to give me a copy of my mortgage` IS
    IF      `the Code applies to the mortgage` `the mortgage`
        AND `the mortgage`'s `is a written mortgage document I signed`
        AND (NOT `the mortgage`'s `is contained in a credit contract I signed`)
        AND (NOT `the mortgage`'s `I have already been given a copy to keep`)
    THEN 14
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 128-130; regs 28HB, 28J, 28JA -- must the lender check I can afford it`

-- s 128: a licensee must not "(a) enter a credit contract with a consumer who will be the debtor", or "(b) increase the
-- credit limit", on a day (the credit day) "unless the licensee has, within 90 days (or other period prescribed by the
-- regulations for the purposes of this section) before the credit day: (c) made an assessment that: (i) is in accordance
-- with section 129; and (ii) covers the period in which the credit day occurs; and (d) made the inquiries and verification
-- in accordance with section 130." Civil penalty: 5,000 penalty units.
-- reg 28J: "For section 128 of the Act, if: (a) the credit to be provided under the credit contract will be used for the
-- purchase of a residential property; and (b) the credit will be secured by a mortgage over the property; the period is
-- 120 days."
-- s 129: the assessment "(a) specifies the period the assessment covers; and (b) assesses whether the credit contract will
-- be unsuitable for the consumer".
-- s 130(1): before the assessment, "(a) make reasonable inquiries about the consumer's requirements and objectives ...; (b)
-- make reasonable inquiries about the consumer's financial situation; and (c) take reasonable steps to verify the
-- consumer's financial situation"; and (d), (e) the prescribed inquiries and steps.
-- reg 28JA: "For paragraph 130(1)(d) of the Act, a licensee must make reasonable inquiries about the maximum credit limit
-- that a consumer requires."
-- s 130(1A): for a small amount credit contract, where the consumer holds an ADI account into which income is credited,
-- "obtain and consider information about each transaction on the account, and the balances of the account, during at
-- least the immediately preceding period of 90 days".
-- reg 28HB(2), (5)-(7): for a small amount credit contract (s 130(1)(e)), the licensee must "ascertain whether the consumer
-- is receiving a payment (a social security payment) under the Social Security Act 1991" and, if so, "obtain, and consider"
-- an income statement and a deduction statement each "issued by Services Australia during the period of 21 days ending on
-- the day on which the licensee considers" it. (Reverse mortgage inquiries, reg 28HA, not encoded.)
-- Whether inquiries were "reasonable" and steps "reasonable" is the licensee's conduct, asked as a fact.
DECLARE `The lender's assessment of me` HAS
    `days before my credit day it was made` IS A NUMBER
    `the credit is to buy residential property and is secured by a mortgage over it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies the period it covers and covers my credit day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable inquiries into my requirements and objectives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable inquiries into my financial situation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable steps to verify my financial situation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable inquiries about the maximum credit limit I require` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is for a small amount credit contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have an ADI account into which my income is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of that account's transactions and balances considered` IS A NUMBER
    `asked whether I receive a social security payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I receive a social security payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `considered Services Australia income and deduction statements each issued within the 21 days before` IS A BOOLEAN

@export How many days before my credit day may the lender's assessment of me be made (s 128, reg 28J)?
GIVEN `buying residential property with a mortgage over it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the credit is to buy residential property and will be secured by a mortgage over that property
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Days before my credit day the assessment may be made` IS
    IF `buying residential property with a mortgage over it`
    THEN 120
    ELSE 90

GIVEN `the assessment` IS A `The lender's assessment of me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the small amount verification steps were taken` IF
        (NOT `the assessment`'s `is for a small amount credit contract`)
    OR  (    (    (NOT `the assessment`'s `I have an ADI account into which my income is paid`)
              OR  `the assessment`'s `days of that account's transactions and balances considered` AT LEAST 90)
         AND `the assessment`'s `asked whether I receive a social security payment`
         AND (    (NOT `the assessment`'s `I receive a social security payment`)
              OR  `the assessment`'s `considered Services Australia income and deduction statements each issued within the 21 days before`))

GIVEN `the assessment` IS A `The lender's assessment of me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 130 inquiries and verification were made` IF
        `the assessment`'s `reasonable inquiries into my requirements and objectives`
    AND `the assessment`'s `reasonable inquiries into my financial situation`
    AND `the assessment`'s `reasonable steps to verify my financial situation`
    AND `the assessment`'s `reasonable inquiries about the maximum credit limit I require`
    AND `the small amount verification steps were taken` `the assessment`

@export Did the lender make the assessment, inquiries and checks it must make before lending to me (ss 128-130)?
GIVEN `the assessment` IS A `The lender's assessment of me` @desc What the lender did to assess you, and when
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the lender assess me as it must` IF
        `the assessment`'s `days before my credit day it was made` AT LEAST 0
    AND `the assessment`'s `days before my credit day it was made` AT MOST `Days before my credit day the assessment may be made` (`the assessment`'s `the credit is to buy residential property and is secured by a mortgage over it`)
    AND `the assessment`'s `specifies the period it covers and covers my credit day`
    AND `the s 130 inquiries and verification were made` `the assessment`

§§ `ss 131, 133, 133BA; reg 28LCF -- is the contract unsuitable for me`

-- s 131(2) (at the time of the assessment) and s 133(2) (at the time the contract is entered or the limit increased): the
-- contract is unsuitable if "(a) it is likely that the consumer will be unable to comply with the consumer's financial
-- obligations under the contract, or could only comply with substantial hardship; or (b) the contract does not meet the
-- consumer's requirements or objectives; or (c) if the regulations prescribe circumstances in which a credit contract is
-- unsuitable--those circumstances apply to the contract".
-- (3): "if the consumer could only comply ... by selling the consumer's principal place of residence, the consumer could
-- only comply with those obligations with substantial hardship, unless the contrary is proved."
-- (3AA): substantial hardship is taken if "(a) the contract is a credit card contract; and (b) the consumer could not comply
-- with an obligation to repay an amount equal to the credit limit of the contract within the period determined by ASIC
-- under section 160F". The ASIC instrument is not deposited: what I could repay within it is an INPUT.
-- s 133BA(1): "A credit card contract is a continuing credit contract under which credit is ordinarily obtained only by the
-- use of a credit card."
-- reg 28LCF(2), for ss 131(2)(c) and 133(2)(c): "A credit contract is unsuitable for a consumer if: (a) the consumer's
-- requirements and objectives are to receive an identified amount of credit; and (b) the credit contract is part of an
-- arrangement by which the identified amount of credit is provided ... by: (i) 2 or more small amount credit contracts; or
-- (ii) 2 or more medium amount credit contracts; or (iii) a combination" of at least 2 kinds; "and (c) the amount that is
-- payable under the combination ... is higher than the maximum amount that could be charged under a single credit contract
-- under section 32A of the Code." That maximum is an INPUT.
-- s 133(1): a licensee must not enter the contract or increase the limit "if the contract is unsuitable for the consumer
-- under subsection (2)". (5): "The regulations may prescribe particular situations in which a credit contract is taken not
-- to be unsuitable" -- none for these contracts was found in the deposited regulations; it is kept as a fact.
-- Simplification: the facts at the assessment and at entry are taken to be the same, so one record serves s 131 and s 133.
-- What is "likely" is the lender's judgment on the information in s 131(4) and s 133(4), asked as a fact.
DECLARE `My position under the contract` HAS
    `likely I will be unable to comply with my obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely I could comply only with substantial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I could comply only by selling my principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contrary of hardship is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a credit card contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `credit limit` IS A NUMBER
    `amount I could repay within the ASIC period` IS A NUMBER
    `meets my requirements and objectives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my objective is an identified amount of credit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is one of 2 or more small or medium amount contracts providing that amount` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount payable under the combination` IS A NUMBER
    `maximum chargeable under a single contract under Code s 32A` IS A NUMBER
    `a regulation takes it not to be unsuitable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the position` IS A `My position under the contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I could comply only with substantial hardship` IF
        `the position`'s `likely I could comply only with substantial hardship`
    OR  (`the position`'s `I could comply only by selling my principal place of residence` AND (NOT `the position`'s `the contrary of hardship is proved`))
    OR  (`the position`'s `is a credit card contract` AND `the position`'s `amount I could repay within the ASIC period` LESS THAN `the position`'s `credit limit`)

GIVEN `the position` IS A `My position under the contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reg 28LCF circumstance applies` IF
        `the position`'s `my objective is an identified amount of credit`
    AND `the position`'s `is one of 2 or more small or medium amount contracts providing that amount`
    AND `the position`'s `amount payable under the combination` GREATER THAN `the position`'s `maximum chargeable under a single contract under Code s 32A`

@export Is the credit contract unsuitable for me (ss 131(2), 133(2), reg 28LCF)?
GIVEN `the position` IS A `My position under the contract` @desc Your circumstances and the contract's terms, amounts in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the contract unsuitable for me` IF
        `the position`'s `likely I will be unable to comply with my obligations`
    OR  `I could comply only with substantial hardship` `the position`
    OR  (NOT `the position`'s `meets my requirements and objectives`)
    OR  `the reg 28LCF circumstance applies` `the position`

@export Does the Act forbid the lender to give me this contract, or to raise its limit, because it is unsuitable (s 133)?
GIVEN `the position` IS A `My position under the contract` @desc Your circumstances and the contract's terms, amounts in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the lender refuse me as unsuitable` IF
        `Is the contract unsuitable for me` `the position`
    AND (NOT `the position`'s `a regulation takes it not to be unsuitable`)

-- s 132(2): if, in the period that "starts on the day (the credit day) the credit contract is entered or the credit limit is
-- increased; and (b) ends 7 years after that day", the consumer asks for a copy of the assessment, the licensee must give a
-- written copy "(c) if the request is made within 2 years of the credit day--before the end of 7 business days after the day
-- the licensee receives the request; and (d) otherwise--before the end of 21 business days". (4): the licensee "must not
-- request or demand payment of an amount for giving the consumer a copy". (s 132(1), a request before entry, not encoded.)
@export Within how many business days must the lender give me a free copy of its assessment of me (0 if the Act gives no right to one then) (s 132)?
GIVEN `credit day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the contract was entered or the limit increased, as YYYYMMDD
      `request received on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the lender received your request, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Business days to give me my assessment` IS
    BRANCH IF `request received on` LESS THAN `credit day`            THEN 0
           IF `request received on` LESS THAN `credit day` PLUS 20000 THEN 7
           IF `request received on` AT MOST `credit day` PLUS 70000   THEN 21
           OTHERWISE 0

§§ `s 133BE -- may my card issuer invite me to raise my limit`

-- s 133BE(1): "A licensee who is the credit provider under a credit card contract must not make a credit limit increase
-- invitation in relation to the contract." Civil penalty 5,000 penalty units. (5): it makes one if it gives the debtor "any
-- form of communication that relates to the contract" and the communication "(i) offers to increase the credit limit ...;
-- (ii) ... invites the consumer to apply for an increase ...; (iii)" was given "for the purpose (or for purposes including
-- the purpose) of encouraging the consumer to consider applying for an increase". The text forbids the invitation; it does
-- not itself set an assessment of the limit, which is s 131(3AA) and s 133(3AA).
DECLARE `Communication to me` HAS
    `from my credit card provider and about my credit card contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `offers to increase the credit limit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `invites me to apply for an increase` IS A BOOLEAN
    `given for a purpose including encouraging me to apply for an increase` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is my card issuer forbidden to send me this communication about raising my credit limit (s 133BE)?
GIVEN `the communication` IS A `Communication to me` @desc A letter, email, call or message from your card issuer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my card issuer forbidden to send it` IF
        `the communication`'s `from my credit card provider and about my credit card contract`
    AND (    `the communication`'s `offers to increase the credit limit`
         OR  `the communication`'s `invites me to apply for an increase`
         OR  `the communication`'s `given for a purpose including encouraging me to apply for an increase`)

§§ `s 5, s 133CA, s 133CC; regs 4D, 28LCA -- is my loan a small amount or short-term credit contract`

-- s 5(1): "small amount credit contract: a credit contract is a small amount credit contract if: (a) the contract is not a
-- continuing credit contract or a low cost credit contract; and (b) the credit provider under the contract is not an ADI;
-- and (c) the credit limit of the contract is $2,000 (or such other amount as is prescribed by the regulations) or less;
-- and (d) the term of the contract is at least 16 days but not longer than 1 year ...; and (e) the debtor's obligations
-- under the contract are not, and will not be, secured; and (f) the contract meets any other requirements prescribed".
-- reg 4D: the credit limit in paragraph (c) "is increased by the amount of each of the following as included in the amount
-- of credit to be provided under the contract: (a) the permitted establishment fee for the contract; (b) the first
-- permitted monthly fee payable under the contract." Note 2: "this regulation could raise a credit limit to a maximum of
-- $2,480".
-- "short-term credit contract": (a)-(c) the same (without reg 4D, which speaks only of the small amount definition), "(d)
-- the term of the contract is 15 days or less; and (e) the contract meets any other requirements prescribed" -- secured or
-- not.
-- s 133CA(1): a licensee must not "(a) enter a short-term credit contract with a consumer", nor increase its limit.
-- s 133CC(1): a licensee must not enter into a small amount credit contract "if the repayments that would be required under
-- the contract would not meet the requirements prescribed by the regulations". (3): if it does, "the consumer is not liable
-- (and is taken never to have been liable) to pay a fee or charge of a kind mentioned in paragraph 31A(1)(a), (b), (c) or
-- (d)" and may recover any paid.
-- reg 28LCA(2): for each repayment period, the repayment plus "any other amounts the consumer is required to pay under any
-- other small amount credit contracts during the repayment period" must be "equal to or less than 10% of the available
-- income the consumer is reasonably expected to receive during the repayment period". (3): "available income" is income
-- less PAYG withholding. The worst repayment period is given.
DECLARE `My loan` HAS
    `is a continuing or low cost credit contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lender is an ADI` IS A BOOLEAN
    `credit limit` IS A NUMBER
    `permitted establishment fee included in the credit` IS A NUMBER
    `first permitted monthly fee included in the credit` IS A NUMBER
    `term in days` IS A NUMBER
    `is secured` IS A BOOLEAN
    `adjusted credit amount` IS A NUMBER
    `refinances credit under another small amount credit contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `establishment fee charged` IS A NUMBER
    `monthly fee charged` IS A NUMBER
    `months of monthly fees charged` IS A NUMBER
    `interest charged` IS A NUMBER
    `repayment in the worst repayment period` IS A NUMBER
    `other small amount loan repayments in that period` IS A NUMBER
    `my available income expected in that period` IS A NUMBER

`the small amount credit limit` MEANS 2000

@export Is my loan a small amount credit contract, a "payday loan" with capped charges (s 5, reg 4D)?
GIVEN `the loan` IS A `My loan` @desc Your loan, with amounts in dollars and its term in days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my loan a small amount credit contract` IF
        (NOT `the loan`'s `is a continuing or low cost credit contract`)
    AND (NOT `the loan`'s `the lender is an ADI`)
    AND `the loan`'s `credit limit` AT MOST `the small amount credit limit` PLUS `the loan`'s `permitted establishment fee included in the credit` PLUS `the loan`'s `first permitted monthly fee included in the credit`
    AND `the loan`'s `term in days` AT LEAST 16
    AND `the loan`'s `term in days` AT MOST 365
    AND (NOT `the loan`'s `is secured`)

@export Is my loan a short-term credit contract (15 days or less) that a licensed lender must not give me at all (ss 5, 133CA)?
GIVEN `the loan` IS A `My loan` @desc Your loan, with amounts in dollars and its term in days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my loan a forbidden short-term credit contract` IF
        (NOT `the loan`'s `is a continuing or low cost credit contract`)
    AND (NOT `the loan`'s `the lender is an ADI`)
    AND `the loan`'s `credit limit` AT MOST `the small amount credit limit`
    AND `the loan`'s `term in days` AT MOST 15

@export Do my small amount loan's repayments stay within 10% of my available income, as they must (s 133CC, reg 28LCA)?
GIVEN `the loan` IS A `My loan` @desc Your loan, with the repayment and income for the worst repayment period, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my repayments within the income limit` IF
    (`the loan`'s `repayment in the worst repayment period` PLUS `the loan`'s `other small amount loan repayments in that period`) TIMES 10
        AT MOST `the loan`'s `my available income expected in that period`

§§ `Code ss 23A, 31A, 31B, 31C, 39B -- what may a small amount loan cost me`

-- Code s 31A(1): a small amount credit contract "must not impose or provide for fees and charges if the fees and charges are
-- not of the following kind: (a) a permitted establishment fee; (b) a fee or charge (a permitted monthly fee) that is payable
-- on a monthly basis starting on the day the contract is entered into; (c) a fee or charge that is payable in the event of a
-- default in payment ...; (d) a government fee, charge or duty". (1A): no permitted establishment fee "if any of the amount
-- of credit to be provided under the contract is to refinance any of the amount of credit provided to the debtor under
-- another small amount credit contract". (2): "A permitted establishment fee is a fee or charge the amount of which must not
-- exceed 20% of the adjusted credit amount". (3): a permitted monthly fee "must not exceed 4% of the adjusted credit amount".
-- Code Dictionary: "adjusted credit amount, in relation to a small amount credit contract, means the first amount of credit
-- that is, or is to be, provided under the contract."
-- s 23A(1): a small amount credit contract "must not impose a monetary liability on the debtor: (a) in respect of an
-- interest charge (including a default rate of interest)"; (b) a prohibited fee; (c) an amount exceeding what the Code
-- allows. (2): the provisions imposing it are void "whether or not the liability is imposed consistently with this Code",
-- and the debtor "may recover as a debt due to the debtor any amount paid".
-- s 31B(1): a credit provider "must not require or accept payment by the debtor of a fee or charge" unless (2) it "may be
-- imposed or provided for by the small amount credit contract under section 31A" or is prescribed. (3): "the debtor is not
-- liable (and is taken never to have been liable) to make the payment" and "may recover as a debt due to the debtor the
-- amount of any payment made".
-- READING (the encoder's, labelled): a fee above the cap is not "a permitted establishment fee" (or monthly fee) at all, so
-- under s 31B(3) the debtor is not liable for ANY of it, not merely the excess. The text never says "to the extent of the
-- excess".
-- s 31C(2): an "unexpired monthly fee" is "each permitted monthly fee that is in respect of a month that commences after the
-- date on which the contract is paid out"; (3) the debtor is not liable for it.
-- s 39B(1): after a default, the credit provider must not "recover more than twice the adjusted credit amount"; (3) "This
-- section does not apply to enforcement expenses."
@export What is the largest establishment fee my small amount loan may charge me (Code s 31A(1A), (2))?
GIVEN `the loan` IS A `My loan` @desc Your small amount loan, amounts in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `The largest establishment fee I can be charged` IS
    IF `the loan`'s `refinances credit under another small amount credit contract`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the loan`'s `adjusted credit amount` TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100

@export What is the largest monthly fee my small amount loan may charge me (Code s 31A(3))?
GIVEN `the loan` IS A `My loan` @desc Your small amount loan, amounts in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `The largest monthly fee I can be charged` IS
    `the loan`'s `adjusted credit amount` TIMES 4 DIVIDED BY 100

@export What is the most the establishment and monthly fees can come to over a number of months (Code s 31A)?
GIVEN `the loan` IS A `My loan` @desc Your small amount loan, amounts in dollars
      `months` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of months for which monthly fees run
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `The most my fees can come to` IS
    `The largest establishment fee I can be charged` `the loan` PLUS `The largest monthly fee I can be charged` `the loan` TIMES `months`

@export Do my small amount loan's charges keep within the caps, with no interest (Code ss 23A, 31A, s 133CC)?
GIVEN `the loan` IS A `My loan` @desc Your small amount loan, amounts in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my loan's charges comply` IF
        `the loan`'s `establishment fee charged` AT MOST `The largest establishment fee I can be charged` `the loan`
    AND `the loan`'s `monthly fee charged` AT MOST `The largest monthly fee I can be charged` `the loan`
    AND `the loan`'s `interest charged` EQUALS 0
    AND `Are my repayments within the income limit` `the loan`

-- The establishment fee and the monthly fees I do not owe: all of them where s 133CC(3) applies; otherwise each one that
-- is above its cap (the READING above); plus any interest (s 23A).
@export How much of what my small amount loan charges am I not liable to pay, and may recover if paid (Code ss 23A, 31B(3), s 133CC(3))?
GIVEN `the loan` IS A `My loan` @desc Your small amount loan, amounts in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much I am not liable to pay` IS
    IF NOT (`Are my repayments within the income limit` `the loan`)
    THEN     `the loan`'s `establishment fee charged`
        PLUS `the loan`'s `monthly fee charged` TIMES `the loan`'s `months of monthly fees charged`
        PLUS `the loan`'s `interest charged`
    ELSE     (IF `the loan`'s `establishment fee charged` GREATER THAN `The largest establishment fee I can be charged` `the loan`
              THEN `the loan`'s `establishment fee charged`
              ELSE 0)
        PLUS (IF `the loan`'s `monthly fee charged` GREATER THAN `The largest monthly fee I can be charged` `the loan`
              THEN `the loan`'s `monthly fee charged` TIMES `the loan`'s `months of monthly fees charged`
              ELSE 0)
        PLUS `the loan`'s `interest charged`

@export After I default on a small amount loan, what is the most the lender may recover from me, before enforcement expenses (Code s 39B)?
GIVEN `the loan` IS A `My loan` @desc Your small amount loan, amounts in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `The most the lender may recover after my default` IS
    `the loan`'s `adjusted credit amount` TIMES 2

@export Is the monthly fee for this month one I need not pay because I paid the loan out before the month began (Code s 31C)?
GIVEN `month starts on` IS A NUMBER @desc The first day of the month the fee is for, as YYYYMMDD
      `paid out on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you paid the loan out, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it an unexpired monthly fee I need not pay` IF
    `month starts on` GREATER THAN `paid out on`

§§ `Code ss 72, 73 -- if I cannot meet my repayments: the hardship notice`

-- s 72(1): "If a debtor considers that he or she is or will be unable to meet his or her obligations under a credit contract,
-- the debtor may give the credit provider notice (a hardship notice), orally or in writing".
-- (2): "Within 21 days after the day of receiving the debtor's hardship notice, the credit provider may give the debtor
-- notice ... requiring the debtor to give the credit provider specified information within 21 days of the date of the
-- notice stated in the notice." (3): "The debtor must comply with the requirement."
-- (4): the credit provider "must, before the end of the period identified under subsection (5), give the debtor a notice"
-- that records that they have agreed to change the contract, or that states they have not agreed, the reasons, and AFCA's
-- details and the debtor's rights. (4A): "Subsection (4) does not apply if the credit provider and the debtor agree to a
-- change to the credit contract that defers or otherwise reduces the obligations of the debtor under that contract for a
-- period not exceeding 90 days."
-- (5) Table -- "Period for giving notice": item 1, "The credit provider does not require information under subsection (2)":
-- "21 days after the day of receiving the hardship notice"; item 2, it requires information "but does not receive any
-- information in compliance with the requirement": "28 days after the stated date of the notice under subsection (2)";
-- item 3, it requires information "and receives information in compliance": "21 days after the day of receiving the
-- information". (6): regulations may shorten these; none was found in the deposited regulations.
-- The Note to (3): the credit provider "need not agree to change the credit contract". Whether it agrees is its choice.
-- s 73(1): a credit provider that agrees a change "as a result of a hardship notice" must, "not later than 30 days after the
-- date of the agreement", give the debtor written notice of the change. (1A): not for a deferral of 90 days or less.
DECLARE `What happened after my hardship notice` IS ONE OF
    `the lender asked me for no information`
    `the lender asked for information and I gave none`
    `the lender asked for information and I gave it`

DECLARE `The day the lender's period runs from` IS ONE OF
    `the day the lender received my hardship notice`
    `the date stated in the lender's request for information`
    `the day the lender received my information`

-- s 72(5) table, as data: item -> (the day the period runs from, the number of days).
@export From which day does the lender's time to answer my hardship notice run (Code s 72(5) table)?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened after my hardship notice` @desc Whether the lender asked you for information, and whether you gave it
GIVETH A `The day the lender's period runs from`
DECIDE `The day the lender's answer period runs from` IS
    CONSIDER `what happened`
    WHEN `the lender asked me for no information`         THEN `the day the lender received my hardship notice`
    WHEN `the lender asked for information and I gave none` THEN `the date stated in the lender's request for information`
    WHEN `the lender asked for information and I gave it`   THEN `the day the lender received my information`

@export Within how many days must the lender tell me whether it agrees to change my contract on hardship grounds (0 if no notice is required) (Code s 72(4), (4A), (5))?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened after my hardship notice` @desc Whether the lender asked you for information, and whether you gave it
      `we agreed a deferral or reduction of 90 days or less` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the lender agreed a change that defers or reduces your obligations for no more than 90 days
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Days for the lender to answer my hardship notice` IS
    IF `we agreed a deferral or reduction of 90 days or less`
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `what happened`
         WHEN `the lender asked me for no information`         THEN 21
         WHEN `the lender asked for information and I gave none` THEN 28
         WHEN `the lender asked for information and I gave it`   THEN 21

@export Must I give the lender the information it asked for about my hardship (Code s 72(2), (3))?
GIVEN `days after my notice the lender asked` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after receiving your hardship notice the lender gave you its request
      `the information is relevant to my inability or how to change the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what it asks for is relevant to whether you can meet your obligations, or how to change the contract
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the lender the information` IF
        `days after my notice the lender asked` AT MOST 21
    AND `the information is relevant to my inability or how to change the contract`

@export Within how many days after we agree a hardship change must the lender give me written notice of it (0 if none is required) (Code s 73)?
GIVEN `the change defers or reduces my obligations for 90 days or less` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreed change is a deferral or reduction for no more than 90 days
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Days for written notice of my hardship change` IS
    IF `the change defers or reduces my obligations for 90 days or less`
    THEN 0
    ELSE 30

§§ `Code ss 88, 89, 89A -- if I default: the default notice`

-- s 88(1): "A credit provider must not begin enforcement proceedings against a debtor in relation to a credit contract
-- unless: (a) the debtor is in default under the credit contract; and (b) the credit provider has given the debtor, and any
-- guarantor, a default notice, complying with this section, allowing the debtor a period of at least 30 days from the date
-- of the notice to remedy the default; and (c) the default has not been remedied within that period". (d), reverse
-- mortgages, not encoded. (2): the same before enforcing a mortgage, taking possession, selling or foreclosing.
-- (3): the notice "must contain a prominent heading at its top stating that it is a default notice and specify" the default,
-- the action to remedy it, the period, the date after which enforcement may begin, and the other matters in (e)-(j),
-- including "the information prescribed by the regulations about the debtor's right to: (i) give a hardship notice". Whether
-- the notice complies is asked as a fact.
-- (5): no notice or wait is required if "(a) the credit provider reasonably believes that it was induced by fraud ...; or (b)
-- the credit provider has made reasonable attempts to locate the debtor ... but without success; or (c) the court authorises
-- the credit provider ...; or (d)" it reasonably believes mortgaged goods are being removed or urgent action is needed.
-- Those are the lender's beliefs and the court's leave, asked as ONE fact.
-- (6): if the credit provider "reasonably believes that a default is not capable of being remedied", the notice need only
-- specify the default, and it may begin "after the period of 30 days from the date of the notice".
-- s 89(1): the debtor "may remedy the default within the period specified in the notice, and the contract or mortgage is
-- then reinstated and any acceleration clause cannot operate." (2): not remedied if, at the end, the debtor is in default
-- "because of the breach specified in the notice or because of a subsequent breach of the same type".
-- s 89A(1), (2): if the debtor gives a hardship notice before or after the default notice, and gave no other in the 4 months
-- before (or the lender reasonably believes the basis is materially different), the credit provider must not begin
-- enforcement unless "(a) the credit provider has given the debtor a notice under paragraph 72(4)(b) ... stating that the
-- credit provider and debtor have not agreed to change the credit contract; and (b) the period of 14 days, starting on the
-- day the credit provider gives the notice under paragraph 72(4)(b), has expired". (Possession of goods under (3) not
-- encoded.) "The period of 14 days, starting on the day" is read as over when 14 or more days have passed since that day.
DECLARE `My default` HAS
    `I am in default` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a complying default notice was given to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days the notice allowed me to remedy` IS A NUMBER
    `days since the date of the notice` IS A NUMBER
    `I remedied the default within that period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lender reasonably believes the default cannot be remedied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an s 88(5) ground applies (fraud, cannot find me, court leave, goods at risk)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I gave a hardship notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I gave another hardship notice in the 4 months before, on the same basis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lender gave me notice that it does not agree to a change` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days since that notice of refusal` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the default` IS A `My default`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the default notice period has run unremedied` IF
        `the default`'s `a complying default notice was given to me`
    AND `the default`'s `days the notice allowed me to remedy` AT LEAST 30
    AND `the default`'s `days since the date of the notice` GREATER THAN `the default`'s `days the notice allowed me to remedy`
    AND (NOT `the default`'s `I remedied the default within that period`)

GIVEN `the default` IS A `My default`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the non-remediable default period has run` IF
        `the default`'s `a complying default notice was given to me`
    AND `the default`'s `the lender reasonably believes the default cannot be remedied`
    AND `the default`'s `days since the date of the notice` GREATER THAN 30

GIVEN `the default` IS A `My default`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my hardship notice holds off enforcement` IF
        `the default`'s `I gave a hardship notice`
    AND (NOT `the default`'s `I gave another hardship notice in the 4 months before, on the same basis`)
    AND (    (NOT `the default`'s `the lender gave me notice that it does not agree to a change`)
         OR  `the default`'s `days since that notice of refusal` LESS THAN 14)

@export May my lender now begin enforcement proceedings against me, or against my mortgaged home (Code ss 88, 89A)?
GIVEN `the default` IS A `My default` @desc Your default, the notice you were given, and any hardship notice you gave, with periods in days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my lender begin enforcement against me` IF
        `the default`'s `I am in default`
    AND (    `the default`'s `an s 88(5) ground applies (fraud, cannot find me, court leave, goods at risk)`
         OR  (    (    `the default notice period has run unremedied` `the default`
                   OR  `the non-remediable default period has run` `the default`)
              AND (NOT `my hardship notice holds off enforcement` `the default`)))

@export If I remedy the default within the period in the notice, is my contract reinstated (Code s 89)?
GIVEN `remedied within the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you remedied the default within the period the notice gave you
      `in default again at the end for the same or the same type of breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the end of that period, you were in default because of the same breach or a later breach of the same type
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my contract reinstated` IF
        `remedied within the period`
    AND (NOT `in default again at the end for the same or the same type of breach`)
